-# React + Vite
+# ConsultTime — faculty consultation
 
-This template provides a minimal setup to get React working in Vite with HMR and some ESLint rules.
+## Local setup
+Requires Node.js compatible with the locked Vite version, npm, and PostgreSQL.
+1. In the project root, run npm ci.
+2. In Backend, run npm ci.
+3. Create an empty PostgreSQL database (for example faculty_consultation).
+4. Copy Backend/.env.example to Backend/.env and fill in database credentials.
+   Generate a random JWT secret with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
+   Put it in JWT_SECRET; never commit the populated .env file.
+5. Back up an existing database first. In Backend, run npm run setup.
+   This runs base-schema.sql and faculty-auth.sql in one transaction. Existing
+   tables/records are retained. Duplicate emails/IDs, incompatible columns, or
+   nonstudent roles cause setup to stop and roll back; review them manually.
+   The baseline is inferred from this project's code, not an export of your database.
+6. Add real faculty directory records to the faculty table using your database tool.
+   No sample accounts or passwords are seeded. Run npm run create-faculty in Backend
+   to provision a login for an existing faculty ID.
+7. Run npm start in Backend. In another terminal, run npm run dev in the project root.
+8. Open the URL Vite prints. Use student registration or the provisioned faculty login.
 
